From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:57:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11345/11362] feat(arc): force turn is a recorded flag, and the
 wire grammar is hashed

Trial 1 hardcoded the force-engine turn to 2. The loop's own default is 3, so
every grammar cell was nudged one turn early and submitted only after the nudge.
Whether the 27B submits on its own was therefore never measured.

- `--force-turn` carries the value, defaults to DEFAULT_FORCE_ENGINE_TURN
  imported from the loop rather than retyped, and lands in trial.json.
- The cell reads the force turn back from the loop's own resolver, because a
  cell is a subprocess and only the env var is authoritative there.
- `first_submission_turn` comes from the per-turn tool names, so "unprompted"
  is read rather than inferred from a nudge counter.
- Each grammar request's grammar text is hashed on the wire. The loop builds
  both grammars once from a deep copy, so a mid-session change should be
  impossible; "should be" is not a measurement, and a grammar that changed
  under a trial would outrank everything else the trial measures.

Trial 1 reproduces with `--force-turn 2`. It was not a default and is not one.

